+
+## 22. Proposed tenant Shipment/POD UI delta — MVP6-SHIPMENT-POD-UI-SCOPE-PREP-01 (unapproved)
+
+This section is a proposed UI expansion. It does not reopen or broaden bounded backend/root acceptance and does not
+turn the pack's existing backend `ready-for-dev` state into UI authority. UI dispatch remains HELD until the exact
+pack target, UI Phase 1.5, immutable source transfer and shared integration patch are separately approved.
+
+### 22.1 Contract-faithful screen surface
+
+The first tenant UI owns only the published operations `queryShipments`, `createShipment`, `getShipment`,
+`transitionShipment` and `captureProofOfDelivery`. It must not add edit/delete/bulk/assignment, standalone lifecycle
+or POD queries, reconciliation, file upload, worker, stock mutation, producer intake or any new backend operation.
+Browser traffic is same-origin to MVC adapters; their only downstream is Gateway port 5000.
+
+The create form has 13 user-entered fields: seven top-level values (`sourceModule`, `sourceType`,
+`sourceDocumentId`, `warehouseReferenceId`, `shipToReference`, `plannedShipAt`, optional `plannedDeliverAt`) and
+six repeatable line values (`lineNumber`, `itemId`, `skuId`, `quantity`, `uomId`, optional
+`inventoryReferenceId`). Therefore `shell: tenant`, `golden_reference: compact`, `form_field_count: 13`.
+There is a separate Create and read-only Details route; no Edit route exists because no edit command is published.
+Transition and POD are bounded action surfaces and do not change the create field count.
+
+### 22.2 Permissions, security and presentation
+
+- Nav/list/detail: `supplychain.shipments.read`; create: `.create`; non-cancel transition: `.dispatch`;
+  Cancelled target: `.cancel`; POD: `.pod.capture`. `reconcile` has no UI action.
+- Missing read renders only UAS-001 access denial. Missing mutation grants remove only the corresponding action;
+  direct MVC/backend invocation remains server-authorized.
+- Tenant and legal entity never appear in UI query/body/form fields. Cross-tenant/cross-LE/deleted/unknown records
+  share the safe 404 presentation.
+- Tenant UI ships en/tr/fr/es/zh/ar/ru, including Arabic RTL and measured responsive states. Wire enum/error tokens
+  are not translated. DataTables v2 and Premium SweetAlert2/shared wrappers are mandatory.
+
+### 22.3 Lifecycle, replay, error and correlation
+
+The UI offers only the frozen lifecycle arrows; the server remains authoritative under races. POD is offered only
+from Dispatched or InTransit and sends evidence reference strings, never binary upload. One logical create,
+transition or POD intent owns one stable idempotency key. Unknown-result retry uses the exact key and payload;
+changed payload is a new intent. Replay is accepted only from the response and is followed by a current-state reload.
+
+Published status/code/body behavior is preserved, including validation, safe 404, 409
+`IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED`, 409 `POD_ALREADY_CAPTURED`, 422 `INVALID_SHIPMENT_TRANSITION` and dependency failure.
+The request/error correlation UUID is a support trace. Detail `lifecycleCorrelationId` is a nullable authoritative
+persisted business root; missing/null is displayed unavailable and never derived from trace or identity.
+
+### 22.4 Ownership and gates
+
+The 28 paths in `docs/roadmap/plans/mvp6-shipment-pod-ui-scope-01/OWNED-PATHS.txt` are the complete prospective
+UI allowlist. Gateway, shared shell, module/permission registration, navigation resources, Program.cs, backend,
+canonical and guard files remain outside it. A single integration owner must bind those shared changes to exact
+preimage/patch/target hashes on an authorized immutable target.
+
+UI Phase 1.5 design is recorded in `PHASE15-ACCEPTANCE.tsv`. Remaining gates are: owner approval and exact
+application of this pack delta; durable source/transfer authority; exact shared integration decision; Phase 1.5
+evidence closure; versioned UI DEV dispatch; writer-complete; and independent browser VER. Until then:
+**UI DEV HELD; UI VER HELD; no UI/shared/gateway write authority.**
